<title>PERU: Peru decres 16 percent public sector pay rise.</title>
<headline>Peru decres 16 percent public sector pay rise.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Peruvian government published a decree Monday granting a 16 percent salary rise for public sector workers.</p>
<p>The salary increase - in the form of a special bonus - will not be incorporated into a worker's basic salary, and so will not be refelected in retirement benefits or Chritsmas pay bonuses.</p>
<p>The increase is retroactive to the beginning of this month.</p>
<p>Cumulative inflation in the 12 month period up to the end of October this year was 11.69 percent.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
